NAME
    units - list test units and compute input cache keys

SYNOPSIS
    units [--kind cargo|dotnet] [--tier T] [--crates] [--rev REV]
          [--repo DIR]
    units --key UNIT [--profile P] [--rev REV] [--repo DIR]

DESCRIPTION
    Command of the emusen.testing module. Derives the catalogue of
    runnable test units directly from repository files at --rev (read
    from git objects, so --rev need not be checked out):

        cargo    Each Cargo root (standalone crate or workspace); with
                 --crates, also emits 'crate' lines for workspace member
                 crates.
        dotnet   Each xunit test class (with [Fact] or [Theory] tests,
                 merged across partial files or inherited from abstract
                 bases), plus 'lunap' for the sibling toolkit suite.

    Each output line is tab-separated: kind, unit, tier tag ('nightly'
    for classes with [Trait("Category", "nightly")], else 'land'), and
    needs.

    With --key UNIT, computes the cache key used by trial(1) reuse from
    the git object IDs of all input directories (unit, dependencies,
    workspace manifest/lock, and declared Testing/inputs.json extras),
    toolchain version (rustc -V or dotnet --version), profile,
    ~/.cargo/config.toml (for cargo), or sibling LunaP commit (for
    dotnet). If any input has uncommitted changes at HEAD, prints 'none'
    and exits 1.

OPTIONS
    --kind cargo|dotnet
        Restrict output to cargo or dotnet units.
    --tier T
        Restrict output to units tagged for tier T.
    --crates
        Include workspace member crates as 'crate' rows.
    --key UNIT
        Print the content hash key and input breakdown for UNIT.
    --profile P
        Cargo profile included in --key computation (default:
        test-fast).
    --rev REV
        Git revision to inspect (default: HEAD).
    --repo DIR
        Git repository root (overrides EMUSEN_REPO).

EXAMPLES
    units --kind cargo | wc -l
    units --tier nightly
    units --crates | grep '^crate' | grep Platform/
    units --key "cargo:EmuSen/Cores/Sony/Sapphire - PlayStation 2"

EXIT STATUS
    0   Catalogue or key printed.
    1   With --key, an input has uncommitted changes (no key computed).
    2   Invalid options, unknown unit, or git error.

SEE ALSO
    impact(1), trial(1), coverage(1), results(1)
